WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.380
A mushroom pops up on a dead log.

2
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.160
It does not walk, swim or fly away.

3
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.340
For a long time, many scientists grouped mushrooms with plants.

4
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.020
Today mushrooms have their own kingdom.

5
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.640
DNA shows they are closer to you than to an oak tree.

6
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.560
How did that happen?

7
00:00:21.383 --> 00:00:23.783
Four clues help scientists sort living things.

8
00:00:24.703 --> 00:00:25.843
Does the cell have a nucleus?

9
00:00:26.783 --> 00:00:29.503
A nucleus is the part of a cell that holds its DNA.

10
00:00:30.523 --> 00:00:31.563
Which cell parts are there?

11
00:00:32.363 --> 00:00:34.663
A cell wall is a stiff layer outside the cell.

12
00:00:35.403 --> 00:00:39.063
A chloroplast is a green part where a cell makes sugar using light.

13
00:00:39.923 --> 00:00:40.963
Is it one cell or many?

14
00:00:41.863 --> 00:00:43.803
Does it make its own food or take food in?

15
00:00:44.733 --> 00:00:49.173
The first clue splits life into cells with a nucleus and cells without one.

16
00:00:50.113 --> 00:00:54.093
Genes and chemistry split the cells without a nucleus into two domains.

17
00:00:55.113 --> 00:00:58.553
So life has three domains: Bacteria, Archaea and Eukarya.

18
00:00:59.513 --> 00:01:02.733
Eukarya holds all organisms whose cells have a nucleus.

19
00:01:03.653 --> 00:01:06.993
Many textbooks use six kingdoms, and four are inside Eukarya.

20
00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.847
A mushroom's cells have a nucleus and a cell wall.

21
00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:15.267
They have no chloroplasts, so a fungus cannot make sugar from light.

22
00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.967
It takes in food from what it grows on.

23
00:01:18.807 --> 00:01:21.727
These clues put fungi in their own kingdom, not with plants.

24
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:28.880
Then came DNA. A DNA sequence is the order of the chemical letters in a stretch of

25
00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:34.900
DNA. When scientists compare the same gene in two organisms, more matches are a clue

26
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.140
to a closer relationship.

27
00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:41.140
A common ancestor is an organism that two groups both descend from.

28
00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:46.340
Comparing DNA and proteins put fungi closer to animals than to plants.

29
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:49.573
That does not make a mushroom an animal.

30
00:01:50.433 --> 00:01:55.413
It means fungi and animals share a more recent common ancestor than either shares

31
00:01:55.413 --> 00:02:00.873
with plants. New tools give new evidence, from microscopes to DNA comparisons.

32
00:02:01.913 --> 00:02:04.413
New evidence can change how living things are grouped.

33
00:02:05.273 --> 00:02:07.653
So DNA can move a living thing to a new group.
